1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:02,673
Your phone rings.

2
00:00:03,533 --> 00:00:06,533
As soon as you see the number, you think, another call from the bank?

3
00:00:06,913 --> 00:00:09,093
Forty calls, fifty calls in a day.

4
00:00:09,553 --> 00:00:11,193
Then the WhatsApp messages begin.

5
00:00:11,553 --> 00:00:12,353
Pay today.

6
00:00:12,953 --> 00:00:14,093
Our person is coming to your house.

7
00:00:14,493 --> 00:00:15,293
We will file a police case.

8
00:00:15,913 --> 00:00:20,173
After a while, even the ringtone makes you tense, doesn't it?

9
00:00:20,233 --> 00:00:21,369
You are sitting with your family,

10
00:00:21,369 --> 00:00:23,193
but your mind keeps going back to the same questions.

11
00:00:23,733 --> 00:00:24,633
What if they call my office?

12
00:00:25,393 --> 00:00:26,613
What if my family finds out?

13
00:00:27,213 --> 00:00:29,153
Even at night, you cannot sleep properly.

14
00:00:30,253 --> 00:00:34,403
If this is happening to you too, pause for a moment.

15
00:00:35,693 --> 00:00:36,573
Take a deep breath.

16
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:38,133
Let's talk calmly.

17
00:00:38,953 --> 00:00:42,993
If you cannot pay your credit card bill, what can the bank actually do?

18
00:00:43,513 --> 00:00:44,333
What are your rights?

19
00:00:44,833 --> 00:00:45,833
How do you handle recovery calls?

20
00:00:47,013 --> 00:00:48,853
When and how can you ask about settlement?

21
00:00:49,173 --> 00:00:52,373
And can your credit score improve afterwards?

22
00:00:52,773 --> 00:00:54,313
We will understand everything, one step at a time.

23
00:00:55,253 --> 00:00:57,133
You do not need to know difficult banking words.

24
00:00:58,053 --> 00:01:00,293
Wherever needed, I will explain them simply.

25
00:01:01,073 --> 00:01:08,463
But let's make one thing clear at the beginning.

26
00:01:08,463 --> 00:01:11,873
If you have the money, paying on time is better.

27
00:01:12,333 --> 00:01:17,293
This video is for people who want to pay but cannot manage it right now.

28
00:01:17,473 --> 00:01:22,753
Your salary has stopped.

29
00:01:25,093 --> 00:01:25,933
Someone at home has needed hospital treatment.

30
00:01:25,933 --> 00:01:27,853
Or the amount has become too big while you were using one card to pay another.

31
00:01:27,933 --> 00:01:30,295
I have the money, but I will not pay, and I want to pay,

32
00:01:30,295 --> 00:01:32,993
but I do not have the money right now, are different situations.

33
00:01:33,593 --> 00:01:37,573
So first, ask yourself honestly: how much can I actually pay?

34
00:01:39,553 --> 00:01:41,613
The problem often starts with something small.

35
00:01:42,553 --> 00:01:43,573
A hospital bill arrives.

36
00:01:43,573 --> 00:01:44,593
You lose your job.

37
00:01:45,013 --> 00:01:46,893
A business customer does not pay on time.

38
00:01:47,753 --> 00:01:50,913
We think, let's use the card now and clear it next month.

39
00:01:51,893 --> 00:01:53,993
But another expense comes next month.

40
00:01:54,713 --> 00:01:56,113
Then we arrange money from another card.

41
00:01:56,113 --> 00:01:58,913
After that, we pay only the minimum due.

42
00:01:58,913 --> 00:02:00,313
Then a small loan.

43
00:02:00,313 --> 00:02:01,713
Then a loan app.

44
00:02:01,973 --> 00:02:04,993
Your salary arrives, and within a few days almost all of it is gone.

45
00:02:05,633 --> 00:02:07,773
Then you think, I am earning money.

46
00:02:07,773 --> 00:02:09,913
Why am I still short every month?

47
00:02:11,353 --> 00:02:12,473
Now, a simple question.

48
00:02:12,753 --> 00:02:17,701
If we keep taking new loans to pay old loans, is our total debt coming down?

49
00:02:17,701 --> 00:02:20,793
Or are we just moving the problem to next month?

50
00:02:21,853 --> 00:02:23,613
The answer may be uncomfortable.

51
00:02:23,613 --> 00:02:27,853
But it tells us what needs to change.

52
00:02:28,193 --> 00:02:31,173
Remember, having debt does not make you a bad person.

53
00:02:32,253 --> 00:02:35,133
One late bill does not reduce your worth.

54
00:02:35,513 --> 00:02:36,976
You have a money problem.

55
00:02:36,976 --> 00:02:37,853
A serious problem.

56
00:02:38,253 --> 00:02:42,853
But it needs a plan, the right information, and support.

57
00:02:43,453 --> 00:02:45,233
Shame will not pay the bill.

58
00:02:45,553 --> 00:02:48,653
A decision made in panic will not help either.

59
00:02:48,853 --> 00:02:50,633
So where should you begin?

60
00:02:50,873 --> 00:02:52,273
Look at your family's essential expenses first.

61
00:02:52,273 --> 00:02:53,073
Food.

62
00:02:53,073 --> 00:02:53,873
Rent.

63
00:02:53,873 --> 00:02:54,673
Medicines.

64
00:02:54,673 --> 00:02:58,553
Your children's school fees.

65
00:02:59,213 --> 00:03:00,233
The basic costs of running your home.

66
00:03:00,233 --> 00:03:01,657
Suppose you make a payment just to stop the calls,

67
00:03:01,657 --> 00:03:02,853
but then have no money left for medicines.

68
00:03:03,953 --> 00:03:05,373
How long can that plan work?

69
00:03:05,813 --> 00:03:07,822
Write down your monthly income.

70
00:03:07,822 --> 00:03:10,233
Under that, write your essential expenses.

71
00:03:10,833 --> 00:03:12,833
Then see how much remains for repayment.

72
00:03:13,613 --> 00:03:15,853
Use paper or make a note on your phone.

73
00:03:16,593 --> 00:03:18,433
Do not keep doing the calculation in your head.

74
00:03:18,433 --> 00:03:22,353
When the numbers are in front of you, the decision becomes clearer.

75
00:03:22,673 --> 00:03:24,593
It is easy to say, I will somehow manage.

76
00:03:26,293 --> 00:03:28,093
Knowing how much you can manage is more useful.

77
00:03:33,243 --> 00:03:34,043
Now, the biggest fear.

78
00:03:34,543 --> 00:03:37,603
If I cannot pay my credit card bill, will the police arrest me?

79
00:03:38,403 --> 00:03:41,429
When genuine money problems prevent payment,

80
00:03:41,429 --> 00:03:46,173
the matter generally concerns recovering the money through civil law.

81
00:03:47,003 --> 00:03:49,263
Missing a payment does not automatically become cheating.

82
00:03:50,103 --> 00:03:52,143
A cheating case depends on the facts.

83
00:03:53,083 --> 00:03:54,143
Was there a plan to deceive from the beginning?

84
00:03:55,243 --> 00:03:56,063
Were fake documents used?

85
00:03:56,743 --> 00:03:58,483
Was incorrect information deliberately given?

86
00:03:59,263 --> 00:04:00,383
Those are different questions.

87
00:04:00,603 --> 00:04:02,638
The Supreme Court has also explained this distinction

88
00:04:02,638 --> 00:04:04,903
between failing to fulfil a payment agreement and cheating.

89
00:04:06,543 --> 00:04:08,959
Someone shouting on the phone that they will file

90
00:04:08,959 --> 00:04:11,423
a criminal case does not decide what the law says.

91
00:04:11,883 --> 00:04:16,423
But that does not mean nothing can happen and you can ignore everything.

92
00:04:16,623 --> 00:04:17,963
The bank can send a legal notice.

93
00:04:17,963 --> 00:04:20,408
It can start a recovery case.

94
00:04:20,408 --> 00:04:24,483
It can use the legal process applicable to your account.

95
00:04:25,743 --> 00:04:28,063
If a court order arrives, you must take it seriously.

96
00:04:29,003 --> 00:04:33,893
Verify a genuine legal notice, court summons, or arbitration notice,

97
00:04:33,893 --> 00:04:35,403
and respond properly.

98
00:04:36,123 --> 00:04:39,923
Speak to a lawyer or ask about legal aid if needed.

99
00:04:40,543 --> 00:04:46,454
The actual document and actual case matter more than a loud voice on the phone.

100
00:04:46,454 --> 00:04:49,607
You may ask, what if a cheque bounced?

101
00:04:49,607 --> 00:04:51,183
Or an auto-debit failed?

102
00:04:51,903 --> 00:04:57,303
Separate legal issues may arise here.

103
00:04:57,963 --> 00:05:01,036
The answer depends on which payment it was, the instructions you gave,

104
00:05:01,036 --> 00:05:02,923
what the notice says, and the actual facts.

105
00:05:03,283 --> 00:05:05,907
Do not assume that no other law can apply

106
00:05:05,907 --> 00:05:09,363
just because the matter began with a credit card bill.

107
00:05:10,243 --> 00:05:11,043
Read the notice.

108
00:05:11,523 --> 00:05:12,323
Understand it.

109
00:05:12,403 --> 00:05:14,143
Get advice when needed.

110
00:05:14,143 --> 00:05:20,373
Now suppose you have dues with four or five banks.

111
00:05:21,013 --> 00:05:23,553
One call has barely ended before another begins.

112
00:05:24,113 --> 00:05:28,353
Sometimes you cannot even remember the exact balance on each card.

113
00:05:28,893 --> 00:05:30,113
Make a list.

114
00:05:31,573 --> 00:05:36,493
For each card, write the bank's name, amount due, due date, and last payment date.

115
00:05:36,993 --> 00:05:39,333
Add any complaint number or legal notice.

116
00:05:40,973 --> 00:05:42,833
Keep each account's papers separately.

117
00:05:42,833 --> 00:05:46,813
Then, when someone pressures you, you will not have to answer from memory.

118
00:05:47,353 --> 00:05:49,153
You will have the facts in front of you.

119
00:05:49,293 --> 00:05:52,793
Settling one card does not automatically settle the others.

120
00:05:53,473 --> 00:05:55,133
Each account must be handled separately.

121
00:05:55,933 --> 00:05:59,593
Do not assume that because your amount is small, the bank will never go to court.

122
00:06:00,693 --> 00:06:05,253
Its decision can depend on the account, its policy, and the legal options available.

123
00:06:06,533 --> 00:06:11,410
Build your plan around checking and responding to genuine communication,

124
00:06:11,410 --> 00:06:15,813
rather than guessing that the bank probably will not do anything.

125
00:06:16,473 --> 00:06:19,840
Now open your statement.

126
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:24,983
Have you ever thought, I stopped using the card, and the bank even blocked it.

127
00:06:24,983 --> 00:06:26,720
Why is the balance still growing?

128
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:29,780
Blocking the card can stop new purchases.

129
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:34,320
But interest and charges applicable to the old balance do not automatically stop.

130
00:06:35,280 --> 00:06:37,160
Do not look only at the final total.

131
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:40,558
How much did you actually spend?

132
00:06:40,558 --> 00:06:42,822
How much is interest?

133
00:06:42,822 --> 00:06:46,220
How much is the late fee?

134
00:06:46,270 --> 00:06:47,070
How much is tax?

135
00:06:47,070 --> 00:06:47,870
And where were your earlier payments adjusted?

136
00:06:47,870 --> 00:06:49,700
If you do not understand, ask the bank for a clear breakdown.

137
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:51,300
Let's take an example.

138
00:06:51,900 --> 00:06:54,000
Suppose the balance is one lakh rupees.

139
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:56,910
At a monthly interest rate of three percent,

140
00:06:56,910 --> 00:07:00,520
a simple calculation gives about three thousand rupees in interest.

141
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:03,380
This is an illustration.

142
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:06,960
Your card's actual rate and calculation may differ.

143
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:08,540
Check your own terms.

144
00:07:09,740 --> 00:07:12,420
Applicable fees and taxes are separate.

145
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:13,661
In that situation,

146
00:07:13,661 --> 00:07:17,200
only a small part of a small payment may reduce what you originally spent.

147
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:20,380
That is why you may think, I keep paying.

148
00:07:20,900 --> 00:07:22,400
Why is the bill not coming down?

149
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:23,960
Now, the minimum due.

150
00:07:25,380 --> 00:07:29,360
Paying the small amount shown on the statement does not clear the whole bill.

151
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:31,580
Interest can continue on the unpaid balance.

152
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,360
Depending on the card's terms, the interest-free benefit may also end.

153
00:07:37,300 --> 00:07:39,580
But the minimum due is not useless.

154
00:07:40,140 --> 00:07:42,242
Paying the full required minimum on time

155
00:07:42,242 --> 00:07:44,660
can prevent the account from becoming overdue.

156
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:50,240
The problem comes when you keep paying only that small amount every month.

157
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:52,740
The debt can continue for a very long time.

158
00:07:52,740 --> 00:07:56,940
If you can afford the full bill, clear it.

159
00:07:57,140 --> 00:08:01,920
If not, ask the bank for a payment option that fits your budget.

160
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:04,940
There is an RBI protection to understand here.

161
00:08:05,300 --> 00:08:06,417
Unpaid taxes, fees,

162
00:08:06,417 --> 00:08:11,120
and other charges cannot simply be added to the principal for charging interest.

163
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:15,880
Principal means the base amount used to calculate interest.

164
00:08:15,880 --> 00:08:16,910
In simple terms,

165
00:08:16,910 --> 00:08:23,220
unpaid charges should not be treated like new spending so that interest keeps being added to them.

166
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:28,361
Also, when checking whether you crossed the limit for an over-limit fee, interest,

167
00:08:28,361 --> 00:08:32,260
taxes, and other charges should not be included in that calculation.

168
00:08:33,280 --> 00:08:37,600
If a charge seems wrong, ask the bank for a written explanation.

169
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:42,320
You do not have to accept it without asking just because it appears on the bill.

170
00:08:42,320 --> 00:08:46,520
Does asking for settlement mean the bank will remove all interest and fees?

171
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:47,960
No.

172
00:08:47,980 --> 00:08:52,140
The bank may agree to reduce some dues, but it is not guaranteed.

173
00:08:52,920 --> 00:08:56,300
It depends on your situation, account, and the bank's approval.

174
00:08:57,400 --> 00:09:02,240
First understand how much you spent, how much you paid, and how much is charges.

175
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:07,580
Then you will know which amount is being discussed during settlement talks.

176
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:11,427
Now check your salary account.

177
00:09:11,427 --> 00:09:15,597
Does your salary come into the same bank where your credit card is overdue?

178
00:09:16,207 --> 00:09:19,427
If yes, read the account and card terms carefully.

179
00:09:20,227 --> 00:09:22,747
You may see words like lien or set-off.

180
00:09:23,167 --> 00:09:26,415
Simply put, depending on applicable terms and law,

181
00:09:26,415 --> 00:09:31,287
the bank may be able to use money in your account with it to pay your dues.

182
00:09:33,067 --> 00:09:36,826
Do not assume that the card and savings account are separate,

183
00:09:36,826 --> 00:09:39,107
so nothing can happen to your salary.

184
00:09:39,107 --> 00:09:42,107
Some agreements give the bank these rights.

185
00:09:42,767 --> 00:09:48,147
Think ahead about the money needed for rent, food, and medicines.

186
00:09:48,587 --> 00:09:51,187
Get advice about your salary account arrangement if necessary.

187
00:09:52,727 --> 00:09:56,207
But receiving your salary in another account does not end the debt.

188
00:09:56,847 --> 00:09:58,667
It does not protect you from every legal recovery step either.

189
00:10:00,007 --> 00:10:02,967
You must follow valid legal duties and court orders.

190
00:10:03,707 --> 00:10:05,373
The point is to understand the risk

191
00:10:05,373 --> 00:10:07,707
and plan properly for your home's basic expenses.

192
00:10:07,707 --> 00:10:13,140
Now, how should you talk to the bank?

193
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:15,840
After so many calls, you feel like switching off the phone.

194
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:17,640
You need some peace.

195
00:10:18,580 --> 00:10:19,740
That feeling is understandable.

196
00:10:20,400 --> 00:10:22,660
But the bank also needs to know your situation.

197
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:27,660
Explain it in writing instead of only talking on calls.

198
00:10:28,060 --> 00:10:29,880
Open the bank's official website.

199
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:33,020
Find the grievance officer's or nodal officer's contact.

200
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:37,340
The names sound complicated, but these are the bank's complaint contacts.

201
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:41,300
Send a simple email explaining why payment has become difficult.

202
00:10:42,020 --> 00:10:45,100
You can write: my income has reduced.

203
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:46,780
There are medical expenses at home.

204
00:10:47,320 --> 00:10:48,640
I want to discuss a payment plan.

205
00:10:49,620 --> 00:10:53,280
After essential household expenses, this is how much I can pay each month.

206
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:55,240
That is enough.

207
00:10:55,300 --> 00:10:56,760
Big words are not necessary.

208
00:10:57,180 --> 00:10:59,460
Be simple and honest.

209
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:02,780
Do not agree to an amount just to end the call.

210
00:11:02,780 --> 00:11:07,040
Saying I will pay tomorrow may bring a few minutes of peace.

211
00:11:08,060 --> 00:11:11,580
But if there will be no money tomorrow, the same problem returns.

212
00:11:11,700 --> 00:11:14,180
Calmly say, I cannot promise this amount.

213
00:11:15,560 --> 00:11:17,020
Please tell me the other options.

214
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:22,495
You can ask about a smaller EMI, a payment plan, changes to repayment terms,

215
00:11:22,495 --> 00:11:23,360
or settlement.

216
00:11:24,180 --> 00:11:27,240
Ask which option is available for your account.

217
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:29,400
Get the details in writing.

218
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:32,780
You can request that most communication happen by email.

219
00:11:33,500 --> 00:11:38,480
But that request does not automatically stop all lawful calls from the bank.

220
00:11:39,760 --> 00:11:41,620
Your preference for email is one thing.

221
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:44,980
Your right to complain about harassment is another.

222
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:50,480
Save all emails, replies, attachments, and complaint numbers in one folder.

223
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:54,020
Will sending an email automatically stop a legal case?

224
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:55,040
No.

225
00:11:55,540 --> 00:11:57,080
But you will have a record.

226
00:11:57,860 --> 00:12:01,429
It will show what you told the bank, which option you requested,

227
00:12:01,429 --> 00:12:03,660
and how you tried to handle the problem.

228
00:12:05,300 --> 00:12:08,860
If there is confusion later, you will not have to prove everything from memory.

229
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:14,373
Now let's talk about recovery agents.

230
00:12:15,433 --> 00:12:17,133
They can contact you about payment.

231
00:12:17,993 --> 00:12:23,727
But that does not mean they can abuse you, threaten you, embarrass you publicly,

232
00:12:23,727 --> 00:12:26,593
or interfere with your family's privacy.

233
00:12:27,353 --> 00:12:32,154
RBI instructions do not allow threatening calls, anonymous calls,

234
00:12:32,154 --> 00:12:35,773
inappropriate messages, or persistent harassment.

235
00:12:36,193 --> 00:12:39,100
Calls to recover overdue payments should not be made before

236
00:12:39,100 --> 00:12:41,613
eight in the morning or after seven in the evening.

237
00:12:43,093 --> 00:12:48,393
And that does not mean they can say whatever they want between eight and seven.

238
00:12:48,393 --> 00:12:50,533
Calling time is one rule.

239
00:12:50,733 --> 00:12:52,493
Harassment is still not allowed.

240
00:12:52,933 --> 00:12:54,873
Someone says, we will tell your neighbours.

241
00:12:55,413 --> 00:12:56,873
We will come to your office and tell everyone.

242
00:12:57,313 --> 00:12:58,113
We will trouble your family.

243
00:12:59,093 --> 00:13:01,533
You do not have to stay silent and accept this as normal recovery.

244
00:13:02,933 --> 00:13:05,413
Calmly ask, what is your name?

245
00:13:05,833 --> 00:13:07,093
Which agency are you from?

246
00:13:07,273 --> 00:13:08,873
Which bank are you calling for?

247
00:13:09,413 --> 00:13:13,033
Send the details of your authorisation from the bank through an official email.

248
00:13:13,913 --> 00:13:16,113
You do not have to be as loud as them.

249
00:13:16,113 --> 00:13:18,553
The goal is not to win an argument.

250
00:13:19,453 --> 00:13:22,813
The goal is to keep a record and handle the problem through the official channel.

251
00:13:24,413 --> 00:13:27,313
You can say, I have explained my situation to the bank in writing.

252
00:13:28,493 --> 00:13:30,533
I will discuss payment through the official channel.

253
00:13:31,193 --> 00:13:33,293
Please do not threaten me.

254
00:13:33,433 --> 00:13:34,233
That is enough.

255
00:13:35,753 --> 00:13:37,493
You do not need a long argument on every call.

256
00:13:38,253 --> 00:13:40,313
Now someone asks for your live location on WhatsApp.

257
00:13:41,293 --> 00:13:42,093
Wait a moment.

258
00:13:42,433 --> 00:13:44,333
Do you know who this person is?

259
00:13:44,333 --> 00:13:46,753
Have you verified that the bank sent them?

260
00:13:47,313 --> 00:13:50,093
Do not send your location simply because someone asks.

261
00:13:51,473 --> 00:13:55,193
Never share your OTP, PIN, password, or secret card details.

262
00:13:56,713 --> 00:13:59,313
Asking for location alone does not prove that someone is fake.

263
00:13:59,813 --> 00:14:03,953
But verify identity before sharing personal information.

264
00:14:04,593 --> 00:14:08,193
A message says, we came to your house, but the door was locked.

265
00:14:08,713 --> 00:14:09,753
First confirm it.

266
00:14:10,253 --> 00:14:11,053
Who came?

267
00:14:11,113 --> 00:14:11,913
When?

268
00:14:11,973 --> 00:14:12,773
From which agency?

269
00:14:12,773 --> 00:14:16,153
Check through the bank's official contact.

270
00:14:16,433 --> 00:14:17,773
Not every message is false.

271
00:14:18,273 --> 00:14:19,373
Not every message is true either.

272
00:14:20,413 --> 00:14:22,393
Do not make a decision only because you are scared.

273
00:14:23,313 --> 00:14:24,393
Check first, then proceed.

274
00:14:25,453 --> 00:14:29,233
Someone says, click this link to see your legal notice.

275
00:14:30,453 --> 00:14:31,933
Do not open an unknown link in panic.

276
00:14:32,853 --> 00:14:37,253
Open the bank's official app or website yourself, or call verified customer care.

277
00:14:38,273 --> 00:14:40,950
But do not assume a notice is fake and

278
00:14:40,950 --> 00:14:44,753
ignore it simply because it came by email or WhatsApp.

279
00:14:45,133 --> 00:14:52,093
Verify the sender, account, case details, and any court or lawyer information.

280
00:14:52,453 --> 00:14:56,313
Taking a few minutes to check is better than clicking in fear.

281
00:14:57,013 --> 00:14:59,648
What if an agent really comes to your house?

282
00:14:59,648 --> 00:15:00,448
Stay calm.

283
00:15:00,773 --> 00:15:03,733
If you are uncomfortable, you do not have to invite them inside.

284
00:15:04,213 --> 00:15:06,933
Ask for ID and the bank's authorisation letter.

285
00:15:07,573 --> 00:15:09,953
Check which account they have come about.

286
00:15:10,313 --> 00:15:13,173
Speak somewhere you feel safe.

287
00:15:13,613 --> 00:15:17,293
Keep a trusted person with you if needed.

288
00:15:18,593 --> 00:15:20,313
There is nothing wrong with having someone there for support.

289
00:15:20,633 --> 00:15:22,797
If they say, sign now, give me cash, or hand over your phone,

290
00:15:22,797 --> 00:15:24,073
do not act just because of pressure.

291
00:15:27,113 --> 00:15:28,553
Do not sign without reading the paper.

292
00:15:29,253 --> 00:15:31,573
If you do not understand, get advice first.

293
00:15:31,833 --> 00:15:35,724
If there is force, a physical threat, or immediate danger,

294
00:15:35,724 --> 00:15:38,273
call the emergency number one one two.

295
00:15:38,553 --> 00:15:40,013
Safety comes first.

296
00:15:40,293 --> 00:15:45,413
But an authorised agent's visit is not illegal simply because a visit occurred.

297
00:15:45,733 --> 00:15:49,873
What matters is how they behaved and whether they followed the proper process.

298
00:15:51,673 --> 00:15:52,713
How do you complain about harassment?

299
00:15:53,753 --> 00:15:56,613
Save dates, times, phone numbers, and messages.

300
00:15:57,453 --> 00:15:58,253
Keep screenshots.

301
00:15:58,853 --> 00:16:00,733
Preserve whatever evidence you have.

302
00:16:01,313 --> 00:16:04,648
Instead of only writing that they are troubling you a lot,

303
00:16:04,648 --> 00:16:06,373
clearly explain what happened.

304
00:16:06,373 --> 00:16:10,993
On this date, at this time, this number called and these words were said.

305
00:16:12,193 --> 00:16:14,093
Details make the complaint easier to understand.

306
00:16:14,253 --> 00:16:17,373
Send it to the bank's grievance team and ask for a complaint number.

307
00:16:18,013 --> 00:16:22,206
If the bank rejects the complaint, you are not satisfied with its reply,

308
00:16:22,206 --> 00:16:24,943
or generally there is no reply for thirty days,

309
00:16:24,943 --> 00:16:28,553
you may approach the RBI Ombudsman under the applicable rules.

310
00:16:30,273 --> 00:16:33,153
Some complaints may have a different prescribed timeline.

311
00:16:33,153 --> 00:16:36,693
Check current rules and the filing deadline before submitting.

312
00:16:37,173 --> 00:16:41,633
The Ombudsman is RBI's process for examining eligible complaints against banks.

313
00:16:41,933 --> 00:16:47,303
The official complaint website is cms dot rbi dot org dot in.

314
00:16:47,303 --> 00:16:49,093
Remember one thing here.

315
00:16:49,193 --> 00:16:51,473
A harassment complaint concerns the recovery method.

316
00:16:52,393 --> 00:16:53,433
It does not automatically cancel your debt.

317
00:16:55,073 --> 00:16:56,673
It does not guarantee a settlement discount either.

318
00:16:57,833 --> 00:17:00,293
But you have the right to ask for fair treatment.

319
00:17:00,293 --> 00:17:02,285
The payment problem and improper recovery

320
00:17:02,285 --> 00:17:04,373
behaviour need to be understood separately.

321
00:17:08,227 --> 00:17:12,347
If calls are disturbing you all day, phone settings can help too.

322
00:17:12,987 --> 00:17:14,667
You can block numbers used for abuse.

323
00:17:16,087 --> 00:17:17,507
Turn on a spam filter.

324
00:17:18,107 --> 00:17:20,247
WhatsApp also has a Silence Unknown Callers option.

325
00:17:21,467 --> 00:17:24,807
But keep a way for the bank to contact you properly.

326
00:17:25,247 --> 00:17:26,467
Check verified emails.

327
00:17:27,227 --> 00:17:28,247
Receive official letters.

328
00:17:28,787 --> 00:17:30,247
Pay attention to genuine legal notices.

329
00:17:30,247 --> 00:17:35,234
If you silence every unknown caller, you could miss an important hospital, job,

330
00:17:35,234 --> 00:17:36,307
or delivery call.

331
00:17:37,687 --> 00:17:40,367
Choose settings according to your daily needs.

332
00:17:41,127 --> 00:17:44,667
Set a regular time to check bank messages and send necessary replies.

333
00:17:46,107 --> 00:17:49,407
Your entire day does not have to be disrupted by every ringtone.

334
00:17:49,987 --> 00:17:53,207
But completely abandoning communication is not a solution either.

335
00:17:53,927 --> 00:17:57,867
Some people ask, if I do not answer calls for sixty days, will the account close?

336
00:17:57,867 --> 00:17:59,947
There is no such guarantee.

337
00:18:00,567 --> 00:18:02,907
One recovery agency's calls may stop.

338
00:18:03,387 --> 00:18:05,047
Another agency's calls may begin.

339
00:18:05,627 --> 00:18:06,847
The team may change.

340
00:18:07,747 --> 00:18:09,527
Fewer calls do not make the debt disappear.

341
00:18:10,147 --> 00:18:14,167
Keep working on your budget, written communication, and payment options.

342
00:18:15,547 --> 00:18:17,087
Do not mistake silence for settlement.

343
00:18:18,007 --> 00:18:22,150
Now let's understand the payment timeline.

344
00:18:23,170 --> 00:18:25,090
Your statement has a due date.

345
00:18:25,090 --> 00:18:27,430
By that date, you need to pay the full bill,

346
00:18:27,430 --> 00:18:29,770
or at least the entire required minimum due.

347
00:18:30,790 --> 00:18:33,290
If the full bill is not paid, interest may apply.

348
00:18:34,150 --> 00:18:38,510
If the full minimum due is also unpaid, the account becomes overdue.

349
00:18:38,590 --> 00:18:39,136
Under RBI rules,

350
00:18:39,136 --> 00:18:43,950
an account must be past due for more than three days before late payment charges are levied or it is reported as past due to a credit bureau.

351
00:18:48,610 --> 00:18:51,690
But the delay is counted from the original due date.

352
00:18:52,150 --> 00:18:54,090
Those three days are not a new due date.

353
00:18:54,090 --> 00:18:58,530
Do not plan payment assuming you will definitely get three extra days.

354
00:18:59,510 --> 00:19:01,470
As the delay grows, recovery calls may increase.

355
00:19:01,930 --> 00:19:04,670
The bank may restrict use of the account or card.

356
00:19:05,230 --> 00:19:06,690
Your credit report may be affected.

357
00:19:07,530 --> 00:19:10,030
Some people say nothing happens for ninety days.

358
00:19:10,870 --> 00:19:12,150
That is incorrect.

359
00:19:12,350 --> 00:19:17,390
Interest, charges, overdue reporting, and recovery follow-up can happen earlier.

360
00:19:19,510 --> 00:19:26,445
If the full minimum amount due on the credit card statement remains unpaid within ninety days from the payment due date,

361
00:19:26,445 --> 00:19:29,450
the account enters the NPA category under RBI rules.

362
00:19:29,870 --> 00:19:32,790
NPA means Non-Performing Asset.

363
00:19:32,970 --> 00:19:34,790
The word is big, but the meaning is simple.

364
00:19:35,290 --> 00:19:37,335
The bank puts the account in a category

365
00:19:37,335 --> 00:19:40,010
where the required payment has not arrived on time.

366
00:19:40,450 --> 00:19:42,970
It then follows the accounting rules for that category.

367
00:19:44,090 --> 00:19:45,210
This does not cancel the debt.

368
00:19:46,290 --> 00:19:49,850
A change in the category's name does not erase the amount you owe.

369
00:19:49,850 --> 00:19:53,927
If the bank offers to convert the balance into EMIs,

370
00:19:53,927 --> 00:19:57,690
check the details before immediately saying yes.

371
00:19:58,110 --> 00:19:59,370
How much must you pay each month?

372
00:20:00,090 --> 00:20:00,890
What is the interest rate?

373
00:20:01,470 --> 00:20:02,590
How many months will it continue?

374
00:20:02,930 --> 00:20:03,730
Is there a processing fee?

375
00:20:04,450 --> 00:20:06,190
How much will you pay in total?

376
00:20:06,750 --> 00:20:08,150
Compare it with your budget.

377
00:20:09,590 --> 00:20:10,830
Can you manage this EMI every month?

378
00:20:11,470 --> 00:20:13,690
If affordable, it may help.

379
00:20:14,110 --> 00:20:15,754
But if it is too high,

380
00:20:15,754 --> 00:20:22,030
agreeing just to escape today's pressure can bring back the same problem next month.

381
00:20:22,250 --> 00:20:24,630
Now another word: write-off.

382
00:20:24,990 --> 00:20:27,710
You hear it and think, good, the bank has removed my debt.

383
00:20:29,510 --> 00:20:33,750
But first understand which kind of write-off the bank means.

384
00:20:34,050 --> 00:20:37,030
A technical write-off is generally a change in the bank's accounting.

385
00:20:37,910 --> 00:20:40,470
It does not mean the bank has forgiven your debt.

386
00:20:41,410 --> 00:20:42,610
Recovery can continue afterwards.

387
00:20:42,610 --> 00:20:45,578
There is no single rule saying that every credit card

388
00:20:45,578 --> 00:20:49,050
will definitely be written off in one hundred and eighty days.

389
00:20:49,190 --> 00:20:51,130
Timing can depend on the bank and account.

390
00:20:52,730 --> 00:20:54,770
Waiting for write-off does not guarantee a large discount.

391
00:20:56,010 --> 00:20:59,770
If you are struggling now, you can ask the bank about workable options now.

392
00:21:00,150 --> 00:21:03,250
Do not sit waiting because you think write-off must happen before settlement.

393
00:21:04,230 --> 00:21:08,727
Every bank's process may differ.

394
00:21:08,727 --> 00:21:13,600
SBI Card, HDFC, ICICI, Axis, YES Bank, Kotak, RBL,

395
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:20,227
and IDFC FIRST do not necessarily have identical internal processes.

396
00:21:20,827 --> 00:21:23,287
Even two customers with the same bank may get different offers.

397
00:21:24,167 --> 00:21:27,967
Your friend says, I settled by paying only twenty-five percent.

398
00:21:28,087 --> 00:21:30,767
That does not mean you will receive the same offer.

399
00:21:31,387 --> 00:21:35,621
The account's age, balance, financial situation,

400
00:21:35,621 --> 00:21:39,327
and what the bank approves can all differ.

401
00:21:39,507 --> 00:21:40,527
Check your own written offer.

402
00:21:41,467 --> 00:21:44,727
Do not treat a percentage someone quoted online as a promise.

403
00:21:45,707 --> 00:21:49,747
Do not believe everything just because the caller speaks nicely either.

404
00:21:50,127 --> 00:21:52,107
A friendly person can give incorrect information.

405
00:21:52,987 --> 00:21:57,087
A rude caller is not a reason to ignore genuine account information.

406
00:21:58,247 --> 00:21:59,487
Verify first.

407
00:21:59,487 --> 00:22:00,727
Then decide.

408
00:22:01,287 --> 00:22:05,513
What actually is settlement?

409
00:22:05,513 --> 00:22:10,193
The bank agrees to accept an agreed amount lower than its total claim.

410
00:22:11,133 --> 00:22:13,753
It waives the remaining amount according to the agreed conditions.

411
00:22:14,933 --> 00:22:18,233
That means it agrees to give up its claim to that remaining amount on those terms.

412
00:22:18,853 --> 00:22:20,953
Both sides need to agree.

413
00:22:21,293 --> 00:22:24,353
Merely sending your request does not create a settlement.

414
00:22:24,853 --> 00:22:26,093
The bank's approval is also required.

415
00:22:26,853 --> 00:22:29,373
You can say, this is what I can arrange now.

416
00:22:30,253 --> 00:22:31,753
I cannot promise more.

417
00:22:32,173 --> 00:22:35,013
Please consider a full and final settlement.

418
00:22:35,213 --> 00:22:37,633
Keep the amount and deadline realistic.

419
00:22:38,473 --> 00:22:43,073
If you need a very expensive new loan to pay the settlement, think for a moment.

420
00:22:43,153 --> 00:22:44,584
Is the problem being solved?

421
00:22:44,584 --> 00:22:46,873
Or will you simply owe someone else now?

422
00:22:47,773 --> 00:22:50,573
An attractive offer and an affordable offer are different things.

423
00:22:52,133 --> 00:22:54,253
Suppose the balance is one lakh rupees.

424
00:22:54,513 --> 00:22:57,653
A caller says, pay thirty thousand and we will close everything.

425
00:22:58,053 --> 00:22:59,853
You feel relieved, right?

426
00:23:00,193 --> 00:23:03,293
But ask for the official settlement letter before paying.

427
00:23:03,293 --> 00:23:07,333
Confirm the offer through the bank's verified customer care.

428
00:23:07,513 --> 00:23:08,573
This is just an example.

429
00:23:09,553 --> 00:23:11,853
There is no guarantee your account will settle for thirty thousand.

430
00:23:12,613 --> 00:23:14,794
A lower amount is useful only when the

431
00:23:14,794 --> 00:23:17,433
offer is genuine and the conditions are clear.

432
00:23:17,853 --> 00:23:22,924
The letter should show your name, account identification, settlement amount,

433
00:23:22,924 --> 00:23:25,793
payment dates, and any instalment schedule.

434
00:23:26,193 --> 00:23:28,236
What happens to the remaining dues after you

435
00:23:28,236 --> 00:23:30,093
pay the agreed amount fully and on time?

436
00:23:30,953 --> 00:23:31,993
Will anything else be claimed?

437
00:23:31,993 --> 00:23:34,313
How will the account appear on your credit report?

438
00:23:35,413 --> 00:23:37,613
Understand these points before paying.

439
00:23:38,093 --> 00:23:40,628
Use an offer from an official bank channel,

440
00:23:40,628 --> 00:23:43,693
or have the bank confirm the letter's authorisation.

441
00:23:44,653 --> 00:23:46,433
Do not pay simply based on a WhatsApp screenshot.

442
00:23:48,253 --> 00:23:51,413
Someone says, pay a little first; we will give you the letter later.

443
00:23:51,913 --> 00:23:54,593
Ask what that payment will count towards.

444
00:23:55,013 --> 00:23:56,073
Is it part of an approved settlement?

445
00:23:56,913 --> 00:23:59,873
Or just an ordinary payment adjusted against the outstanding balance?

446
00:24:00,693 --> 00:24:04,222
You should not discover later that the caller said

447
00:24:04,222 --> 00:24:08,173
one thing but the bank recorded the payment differently.

448
00:24:08,493 --> 00:24:10,973
The payment's purpose should be clear beforehand.

449
00:24:11,493 --> 00:24:14,213
Pay only using a method authorised by the bank.

450
00:24:15,053 --> 00:24:17,833
Use its official app, website, or a channel the bank has confirmed.

451
00:24:19,633 --> 00:24:23,173
Do not send money to an agent's personal UPI account.

452
00:24:23,313 --> 00:24:24,573
Do not hand over cash.

453
00:24:25,233 --> 00:24:26,033
Keep the receipt.

454
00:24:26,033 --> 00:24:29,223
If there are instalments, follow the dates carefully.

455
00:24:30,393 --> 00:24:33,153
Ask beforehand what happens if you miss one instalment.

456
00:24:34,473 --> 00:24:37,533
Sometimes a missed payment can break the settlement conditions.

457
00:24:38,233 --> 00:24:41,493
The dates matter as well as the total amount.

458
00:24:41,913 --> 00:24:45,033
After completing all payments, get written confirmation.

459
00:24:45,613 --> 00:24:50,273
Ask for the applicable No Dues Certificate or settlement completion certificate.

460
00:24:50,693 --> 00:24:55,633
If a court case is already running, confirm how it will be closed.

461
00:24:56,173 --> 00:24:58,713
A phone assurance saying do not worry, we will do it, is not enough.

462
00:24:59,873 --> 00:25:04,533
There should be a proper closure record according to the final agreement.

463
00:25:05,313 --> 00:25:06,433
Now, Lok Adalat.

464
00:25:07,933 --> 00:25:09,073
Some people become nervous hearing the name.

465
00:25:09,613 --> 00:25:10,413
Will I have to go to court?

466
00:25:10,873 --> 00:25:11,753
What will they ask?

467
00:25:12,213 --> 00:25:14,128
A regular Lok Adalat gives both sides an

468
00:25:14,128 --> 00:25:16,473
opportunity to discuss and agree on a settlement.

469
00:25:18,013 --> 00:25:20,978
An eligible matter can reach it before a court case,

470
00:25:20,978 --> 00:25:22,973
or while a case is already running.

471
00:25:22,973 --> 00:25:26,413
Listen to the offer.

472
00:25:26,413 --> 00:25:28,993
Read the terms.

473
00:25:29,043 --> 00:25:29,843
Check whether you can afford them.

474
00:25:29,843 --> 00:25:32,973
You do not have to accept every offer simply because you went there.

475
00:25:33,633 --> 00:25:36,833
In a regular Lok Adalat, both sides' agreement is required.

476
00:25:37,133 --> 00:25:43,373
But once an agreed settlement becomes a Lok Adalat award, it is final and binding.

477
00:25:44,073 --> 00:25:46,653
It has legal effect like a civil court decree.

478
00:25:47,173 --> 00:25:49,353
It is not merely a conversation after which you leave.

479
00:25:50,153 --> 00:25:51,253
You must follow it.

480
00:25:51,253 --> 00:25:52,993
There is no ordinary appeal route.

481
00:25:54,313 --> 00:25:57,313
Do not sign without understanding the amount, dates, and consequences.

482
00:25:59,833 --> 00:26:04,173
You can ask, after I complete this payment, will anything else remain?

483
00:26:04,793 --> 00:26:06,093
What happens if I miss one payment?

484
00:26:07,113 --> 00:26:07,993
What will be updated in the credit report?

485
00:26:09,233 --> 00:26:10,553
These are completely reasonable questions.

486
00:26:11,173 --> 00:26:12,693
Ask again if you do not understand.

487
00:26:13,553 --> 00:26:16,293
It is better to get clarity first than to say yes under pressure.

488
00:26:19,933 --> 00:26:21,693
After settlement, the next worry arrives.

489
00:26:21,693 --> 00:26:23,793
What happens to my CIBIL score?

490
00:26:24,713 --> 00:26:26,773
Will I ever get another loan?

491
00:26:26,953 --> 00:26:28,693
Settlement can affect future approvals.

492
00:26:30,053 --> 00:26:32,833
But do not assume your financial life is over.

493
00:26:33,253 --> 00:26:36,473
First understand two words: Settled and Closed.

494
00:26:36,833 --> 00:26:37,693
They are not the same.

495
00:26:38,413 --> 00:26:42,133
Settled generally means the lender accepted less than the full dues.

496
00:26:43,773 --> 00:26:48,013
Closed is a different status, generally associated with full repayment.

497
00:26:48,013 --> 00:26:54,193
When deciding on a new loan or card, a lender may view a Settled status negatively.

498
00:26:54,493 --> 00:26:57,093
Receiving a No Dues Certificate does not necessarily

499
00:26:57,093 --> 00:26:59,793
mean the credit report will automatically show Closed.

500
00:27:00,293 --> 00:27:02,573
Completing the settlement payment is one thing.

501
00:27:03,053 --> 00:27:05,993
The status in the credit report is another.

502
00:27:06,393 --> 00:27:07,713
You need to check both.

503
00:27:08,833 --> 00:27:10,933
Can you improve your credit again?

504
00:27:11,593 --> 00:27:13,653
Yes, but there is no instant reset.

505
00:27:14,553 --> 00:27:17,633
First make your income and household budget more stable.

506
00:27:17,953 --> 00:27:19,613
Try to build a small emergency fund.

507
00:27:20,833 --> 00:27:22,285
If the old debt has been settled,

508
00:27:22,285 --> 00:27:24,573
you do not need a new credit card the very next day.

509
00:27:25,753 --> 00:27:27,833
Give yourself some breathing space first.

510
00:27:28,493 --> 00:27:30,313
Then decide what to do next based on your situation.

511
00:27:31,873 --> 00:27:34,216
Later, if your needs and budget allow it,

512
00:27:34,216 --> 00:27:36,673
you can consider an FD-backed secured card.

513
00:27:37,313 --> 00:27:39,893
This is a credit card issued against a fixed deposit.

514
00:27:43,993 --> 00:27:45,648
The bank decides who is approved, how much deposit is needed,

515
00:27:45,648 --> 00:27:46,353
and what limit is offered.

516
00:27:47,093 --> 00:27:49,233
Simply making a fixed deposit does not guarantee approval.

517
00:27:50,333 --> 00:27:53,753
Do not lock all your emergency savings away just to get a new card.

518
00:27:55,013 --> 00:27:57,653
Money you need in an emergency should remain available too.

519
00:27:58,633 --> 00:28:02,653
If you get a card, use it for small, planned expenses.

520
00:28:03,693 --> 00:28:04,993
Pay the full bill by the due date.

521
00:28:06,153 --> 00:28:07,993
Keep spending low and affordable.

522
00:28:07,993 --> 00:28:12,873
Using ten or twenty percent of the limit may be manageable for some people.

523
00:28:13,773 --> 00:28:16,513
But no exact percentage guarantees a higher score.

524
00:28:20,513 --> 00:28:23,029
What matters is paying on time, spending within your budget,

525
00:28:23,029 --> 00:28:24,832
avoiding repeated unnecessary applications,

526
00:28:24,832 --> 00:28:26,593
and regularly checking your credit report.

527
00:28:27,673 --> 00:28:31,453
After settlement, check whether the bank updated the report.

528
00:28:31,573 --> 00:28:32,373
Is the balance incorrect?

529
00:28:32,713 --> 00:28:33,593
Is the overdue status wrong?

530
00:28:34,093 --> 00:28:35,413
Does the same account appear twice?

531
00:28:35,413 --> 00:28:37,973
Raise a dispute with the bank and credit bureau.

532
00:28:39,513 --> 00:28:41,973
A dispute is a request to correct an inaccurate entry.

533
00:28:43,133 --> 00:28:44,908
But negative history that is correct does

534
00:28:44,908 --> 00:28:46,813
not disappear merely because you request it.

535
00:28:47,993 --> 00:28:52,993
Correcting a report's error and erasing an accurate old record are different things.

536
00:28:54,073 --> 00:28:59,105
Be careful with promises that your score will reach seven hundred and fifty in eighteen months,

537
00:28:59,105 --> 00:29:01,753
or everything will be clean in twenty-four months.

538
00:29:01,753 --> 00:29:05,313
Nobody can promise that for every person.

539
00:29:06,013 --> 00:29:10,913
Your earlier history, current accounts, payments, and reporting all matter.

540
00:29:11,433 --> 00:29:17,353
Instead of chasing a fixed date, build habits you can follow over time.

541
00:29:17,993 --> 00:29:20,693
One difficult phase does not decide your whole life.

542
00:29:21,813 --> 00:29:23,793
If you are scared, or do not know how to tell your family,

543
00:29:23,793 --> 00:29:24,783
start with someone you trust.

544
00:29:24,783 --> 00:29:26,763
Someone in your family you feel safe with, or a close friend.

545
00:29:26,763 --> 00:29:28,413
You do not have to carry the entire problem alone.

546
00:29:28,463 --> 00:29:29,263
You can say, I am having money problems.

547
00:29:29,263 --> 00:29:30,063
These are my dues.

548
00:29:30,063 --> 00:29:36,973
This is my income.

549
00:29:36,973 --> 00:29:49,813
I want to follow this plan.

550
00:29:49,813 --> 00:30:00,807
I need some support.

551
00:30:00,857 --> 00:30:01,657
Asking for support is not a weakness.

552
00:30:01,657 --> 00:30:02,457
Talking to the right person can ease some pressure and help you think.

553
00:30:02,457 --> 00:30:03,257
Let's put the whole explanation into eight simple steps.

554
00:30:03,257 --> 00:30:04,827
Step one: list every card and balance in one place.

555
00:30:05,167 --> 00:30:07,987
Check your income, essential expenses, and money available for repayment.

556
00:30:09,807 --> 00:30:14,427
Check the salary account terms too, and any risk from dues with that same bank.

557
00:30:14,987 --> 00:30:17,647
Clear numbers make the plan realistic.

558
00:30:18,467 --> 00:30:20,279
Step two: explain your situation in

559
00:30:20,279 --> 00:30:23,127
writing through each bank's official complaint channel.

560
00:30:23,127 --> 00:30:27,387
Ask for a payment option you can afford.

561
00:30:27,627 --> 00:30:29,527
Save replies and complaint numbers.

562
00:30:30,587 --> 00:30:33,087
Step three: manage calls through phone settings.

563
00:30:34,287 --> 00:30:38,747
But keep checking verified bank emails, letters, and genuine legal notices.

564
00:30:39,907 --> 00:30:45,427
Step four: examine the full cost before taking a new loan to pay old debt.

565
00:30:46,047 --> 00:30:50,447
Understand what minimum payments do and how much interest may continue.

566
00:30:51,047 --> 00:30:52,047
Do not promise more than your budget allows.

567
00:30:53,887 --> 00:30:58,627
Step five: save evidence of threats or harassment and complain.

568
00:31:00,447 --> 00:31:03,007
Use the RBI complaint process according to your needs and eligibility.

569
00:31:04,627 --> 00:31:06,147
If there is immediate danger, call one one two.

570
00:31:06,987 --> 00:31:11,827
Step six: NPA, write-off, and settlement are three different things.

571
00:31:12,207 --> 00:31:14,007
Write-off does not cancel the debt.

572
00:31:14,487 --> 00:31:17,507
Ask the bank about options that are available and affordable now.

573
00:31:20,087 --> 00:31:20,947
Step seven: verify the settlement letter.

574
00:31:21,387 --> 00:31:26,187
Make the amount, dates, waiver of remaining dues, and credit reporting clear.

575
00:31:26,187 --> 00:31:27,347
Pay through an authorised method.

576
00:31:28,387 --> 00:31:30,327
Keep receipts and get confirmation of completion.

577
00:31:31,467 --> 00:31:34,287
Step eight: work on making your income stable.

578
00:31:35,007 --> 00:31:36,867
Build emergency savings.

579
00:31:36,867 --> 00:31:37,867
Check your credit report.

580
00:31:38,627 --> 00:31:43,440
If you later use suitable credit for your needs, use it carefully.

581
00:31:43,440 --> 00:31:45,847
Pay the full bill on time.

582
00:31:45,847 --> 00:31:49,187
These actions gradually build a better routine.

583
00:31:49,827 --> 00:31:52,527
Now ask yourself, what can I do today?

584
00:31:53,287 --> 00:31:54,807
You do not have to solve the entire problem today.

585
00:31:55,827 --> 00:31:57,367
But can you take one useful step?

586
00:31:58,207 --> 00:31:59,287
List your accounts?

587
00:32:00,367 --> 00:32:01,287
Check one statement?

588
00:32:02,327 --> 00:32:03,127
Send one email?

589
00:32:03,967 --> 00:32:05,307
Speak to someone you trust?

590
00:32:06,567 --> 00:32:07,587
Start there.

591
00:32:08,307 --> 00:32:11,547
When one task becomes clear, the next one can feel a little easier.

592
00:32:12,547 --> 00:32:14,267
You owe money.

593
00:32:14,267 --> 00:32:15,067
That is true.

594
00:32:15,067 --> 00:32:17,347
But you also have the right to be treated with respect.

595
00:32:17,687 --> 00:32:20,147
Understand your responsibility honestly.

596
00:32:20,427 --> 00:32:21,907
Know your rights too.

597
00:32:22,047 --> 00:32:23,067
Both can exist together.

598
00:32:24,507 --> 00:32:25,507
You do not have to live only in fear.

599
00:32:26,047 --> 00:32:29,485
You can move forward by understanding the facts, keeping records,

600
00:32:29,485 --> 00:32:30,967
and making a realistic plan.

601
00:32:31,787 --> 00:32:34,567
I want to share something personal too.

602
00:32:34,827 --> 00:32:37,247
I am also handling this kind of situation right now.

603
00:32:37,727 --> 00:32:41,187
That is why I understand how tiring this pressure can be.

604
00:32:41,187 --> 00:32:43,787
In the next video, I will show my actual process.

605
00:32:44,327 --> 00:32:45,667
How I talk to the banks.

606
00:32:46,127 --> 00:32:47,407
Which letters I send.

607
00:32:47,687 --> 00:32:48,767
What replies arrive.

608
00:32:49,107 --> 00:32:50,947
And which decisions I make.

609
00:32:51,207 --> 00:32:53,447
Your case may be different from mine.

610
00:32:54,087 --> 00:32:58,587
But seeing the process may help you ask the right questions about your account.

611
00:32:59,907 --> 00:33:02,907
Subscribe so that you do not miss the next video.

612
00:33:03,387 --> 00:33:05,927
Tap the bell icon and select All notifications.

613
00:33:07,007 --> 00:33:12,357
If this explanation helped, share it with someone who needs it.

614
00:33:12,727 --> 00:33:17,787
They may be handling the same stress alone and unable to tell anyone.

615
00:33:18,467 --> 00:33:23,227
Your message could help them pause, think, and take their first useful step.
